+**Ending**: how a run finished, written when it happens — accepted, turned down, refused to the end, done, fallen over, or stopped. *Done* is a run with nothing to accept or turn down, which is what reading a report is. *Stopped* is a run the user moved past before answering it: a correction or a new ask mid-plan or over its proposal, whose run follows it in the same negotiation, or a report of the workout its adaptation was for. A run that is waiting on an answer has no ending, and neither has one that was cut.
 
